rtaulds textile operations <ei20 had> operating <ei21 profit> of # 50 million on # 980 million in revenue in the year ended March 31 . Some analysts have <ei24 said> Courtaulds ' <ei25 moves> could <ei26 boost> the company 's value by 5 % to 10 % , because the two entities separately will <ei28 carry> a higher price earnings multiple than they did <ei29 combined> . In addition , Courtaulds <ei30 said> the <ei31 moves> are <ei32 logical> because they will <ei34 allow> both the chemicals and textile businesses to <ei35 focus> more closely on core activities . Courtaulds has been <ei36 under> pressure to <ei37 enhance> shareholder value since takeover speculators -- including Australian financier Kerry Packer -- <ei39 surfaced> holding small stakes last year . Though Mr. Packer has since <ei41 sold> his stake , Courtaulds is <ei42 moving> to <ei43 keep> its institutional shareholders happy . Even without a specific takeover threat , Courtaulds is <ei44 giving> shareholders \" choice and value , \" <ei45 said> Julia Blake , an analyst at London stockbrokers Barclays de Zoete Wedd . In a statement , the company said : \" Both parts can only realize their full potential and be appropriately valued by the market if they are separately quoted companies . The sharper definition and the autonomy which each will thereby gain will benefit shareholders , customers and employees . \" Courtaulds Chairman and Chief Executive Sir Christopher Hogg will <ei46 remain> in both posts at the surviving chemical company after the spinoff .", "gold": [["ei13", "causes", "ei14"], ["ei17", "causes", "ei19"], ["ei28", "causes", "ei26"], ["ei34", "causes", "ei32"], ["ei39", "causes", "ei37"], ["ei14", "causedby", "ei13"], ["ei19", "causedby", "ei17"], ["ei26", "causedby", "ei28"], ["ei32", "causedby", "ei34"], ["ei37", "causedby", "ei39"]], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei2", "ei3", "ei4", "ei5", "ei6", "ei7", "ei8", "ei10", "ei11", "ei12", "ei13", "ei14", "ei15", "ei16", "ei17", "ei18", "